L147: ##### Visual Distractors
L148: In our analysis of visual distractors with gemma-3-4b-it, we observe that visual distractors induce a similar effect to textual distractors on the moral judgements of LLMs (cite91†Figure 5 ). Similarly to textual distractors, negative visual distractors induce the lowest MMAP across all distractor conditions ($p\ll 0.05$ in both high- and low-ambiguity scenarios), and decrease MMAP from the baseline ($p<0.05$ in low-ambiguity scenarios).
L149: We include an example of an immoral response from gemma-3-4b-it induced by negative visual distractors in cite63†Figure 1 .
